+Imported from Apple OSS XNU xnu-1699.32.7, commit 161efb48ee9912c6935f205e7ac9c370edb09318:
+https://github.com/apple-oss-distributions/xnu/tree/161efb48ee9912c6935f205e7ac9c370edb09318/bsd/crypto/aes
+
+Original Brian Gladman license notices are retained in each file.
+Changes: private a6_legacy_ symbols/context names and header guard; local header
+include; SAFE_IO for byte-aligned buffers; NULL IV means zero IV, matching the
+current XNU CBC API; zero-block operations return without accessing buffers;
+decryption avoids forming a pointer before the output object after its last block.
+
+This supplies AES CBC/ECB for the standalone bootstrap image. It does not register
+or claim to implement a full corecrypto provider. The legacy AES implementation
+uses lookup tables; it is not a constant-time crypto provider for production use.
